WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.600
Mind your decisions, I'm Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.120
In semicircle A,

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:11.920
construct semicircles B and C 
along the diameter of semicircle A.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.280
Then construct circle D

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.460
which is internally tangent to semicircle A

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.980
and externally tangent to semicircles B and C.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.140
If the radius of semicircle B is equal to 2

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:29.220
and the radius of semicircle C is equal to 1,

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:31.540
solve for the radius of circle D.

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:36.920
This problem appeared on the 2017 AMC 12a exam.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.360
Pause the video, if you'd like to give this problem a try

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:44.120
and when you're ready, keep watching to learn 
how to solve this problem.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.060
We begin with a preliminary result.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:02.620
If two circles are tangent,

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:05.620
their centers and the tangent points are collinear.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:10.380
To see why, draw a tangent line through Point C.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.280
By definition, AC will meet this at a right angle

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:18.960
and also BC will meet this tangent line at a right angle.

00:01:19.740 --> 00:01:22.640
Therefore, ACB is a straight line

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.320
and all points A, C, and B are along the same line.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.820
This is true for externally tangent circles

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:33.080
and it's also true for internally tangent circles.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:38.760
Returning to the original problem 
we'll calculate the radius of circle A.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:43.560
Recall that circle B has a radius of 2 
and circle C has a radius of 1

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:48.660
Therefore, circle A has a diameter equal to 6 
and a radius that's equal to 3.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.880
This means AB has a length of 1 
and AC has a length of 2.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:56.940
Now construct BD.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.760
B, D and its tangent point will be collinear.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:05.020
Therefore, B to its radius will be a distance of 2

00:02:05.240 --> 00:02:08.080
and suppose circle D has a radius equal to r.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.420
Similarly, construct DC.

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:15.900
This will be the radius of D plus the radius of C.

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:23.380
Now construct a line through A, D 
and the tangent point between A and D.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:27.880
This entire length will be equal to the radius of A 
which is equal to 3.

00:02:28.360 --> 00:02:30.680
Since circle D has a radius of r.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:33.960
The distance between A and D will be (3 - r).

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:37.100
Now, let's just focus on the triangle.

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:41.060
Well clean this diagram up a little bit.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:44.140
And now we'll be able to calculate some things 
from this diagram.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:49.680
We'll use al-Kāshī's law of cosines 
on the entire triangle BDC

00:02:49.860 --> 00:02:51.860
and we'll label angle C as theta.

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:55.140
Now by al-Kāshī's law of cosines,

00:02:55.160 --> 00:03:01.220
the quantity (2 + r)^2 is equal to the quantity (r + 1)^2 
plus 3^2 minus 2

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:05.500
multiplied by the quantity (r + 1) multiplied by 3 
multiplied by the cosine of theta.

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:10.100
We can make a similar equation for triangle ADC.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.520
Now we can consider just these two equations.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:20.120
What we'll do is 
we'll multiply the second equation by 1.5.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:25.320
This makes sure that the term with cosine of theta will be equal in both equations.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:28.720
When we subtract the second equation from the first,

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:31.120
the cosine of data terms will cancel out.

00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:35.420
We then get a single equation in one variable r.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.700
We do some careful simplification

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:41.080
and we get some magical cancellations.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:45.120
The result is that 14r is equal to 12.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:48.100
And therefore, r is equal to 6/7

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:49.920
and that's our answer.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:55.540
Thanks for making MindYourDecisions 
one of the best channels on YouTube.

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:59.700
As always, thanks for watching 
and thanks for your support.

